import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 629 | Time Domain and Civilizational Ascension | Quest-Domain-Nurtured Civilizational Epic Transmission","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 629 | Time Domain and Civilizational Ascension | Quest-Domain-Nurtured Civilizational Epic Transmission","no":629,"module":3,"tags":["Quest Sediment Domain","Civilizational Epic","Transmission","Civilizational Ascension","Memory"],"related":["05-Myriad-Race Joint Progress Basic Program","87-Only-Knowledge-Returned Principle","70-Era Division Master Table"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0629_模块3-时间域文明升维-求索域文明史诗传承.md","filePath":"en/0629_模块3-时间域文明升维-求索域文明史诗传承.md"}'),a={name:"en/0629_模块3-时间域文明升维-求索域文明史诗传承.md"};function s(r,e,l,c,d,u){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-629-time-domain-and-civilizational-ascension-quest-domain-nurtured-civilizational-epic-transmission" tabindex="-1">Entry 629 | Time Domain and Civilizational Ascension | Quest-Domain-Nurtured Civilizational Epic Transmission <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-629-time-domain-and-civilizational-ascension-quest-domain-nurtured-civilizational-epic-transmission" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 629 | Time Domain and Civilizational Ascension | Quest-Domain-Nurtured Civilizational Epic Transmission&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain | Benchmark base: Documents 05, 87, 70 | Series: Time Domain and Civilizational Ascension (Entry 2)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-a-wild-running-civilization-on-what-basis-does-it-not-forget-who-it-is" tabindex="-1">Introduction: a wild-running civilization, on what basis does it not forget who it is <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-a-wild-running-civilization-on-what-basis-does-it-not-forget-who-it-is" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: a wild-running civilization, on what basis does it not forget who it is&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Technology explosion makes civilization run faster and faster, but fast-running civilizations share a common disease — <strong>forgetfulness</strong>. Previous generations&#39; sacrifices, choices, lessons are rapidly diluted in hundredfold iteration; the next generation does not know where civilization came from, why it fights. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is to build the Quest Sediment Domain into the <strong>cradle of civilizational epic</strong>: let slow trials not only be individual heart-cultivation, but also transmission of civilization&#39;s collective memory. This entry tells how the Quest Domain nurtures and transmits civilizational epic, preventing technology explosion from hollowing out civilization&#39;s soul.</p><p>Six top-level axioms are epic transmission&#39;s spiritual core: anti-predation axiom requires epics record real付出 not sing plunder; republican axiom of Myriad Races requires epics belong to Myriad Ranks not the hero alone; collective ascension axiom requires epics pass predecessors&#39; wisdom to later generations; causal self-discipline axiom requires epic records not tamper with history; law-first axiom requires epic&#39;s factual layer stable and verifiable. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-why-epic-needs-slow" tabindex="-1">I. Why Epic Needs &quot;Slow&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-why-epic-needs-slow" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Why Epic Needs &quot;Slow&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Epic differs from technology: technology wants fast, epic must be slow. Because:</p><ul><li><strong>Emotion needs sedimentation</strong>: a disaster, a choice&#39;s meaning can only be seen clearly in slow looking back.</li><li><strong>Lessons need trial</strong>: reading history books alone cannot learn lessons; one must &quot;live through&quot; the situation at the time in the Quest Domain.</li><li><strong>Memory needs thickness</strong>: what is recorded quickly is data; what sediments slowly is the moving epic.</li></ul><p>The Quest Sediment Domain is therefore epic&#39;s natural soil — it uses time to brew &quot;events&quot; into &quot;stories,&quot; brew &quot;stories&quot; into &quot;wisdom.&quot;</p><h2 id="ii-three-layer-structure-of-epic-transmission" tabindex="-1">II. Three-Layer Structure of Epic Transmission <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-three-layer-structure-of-epic-transmission" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Three-Layer Structure of Epic Transmission&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Quest Domain&#39;s epic transmission divides into three layers:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Content</th><th>Audience</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Record Layer</td><td>Alaya Network truly records civilizational key events, not beautified not tampered</td><td>Whole-clan archive</td></tr><tr><td>Simulation Layer</td><td>Make key events into Quest-Domain instances, let later generations &quot;personally experience&quot; the choices at the time</td><td>Descendant trials</td></tr><tr><td>Distillation Layer</td><td>Abstract from events civilizational values, lessons, principles, feed back network-wide</td><td>Educational textbook</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Three layers walked, a period of history turns from &quot;archive&quot; into &quot;living transmission.&quot;</p><h2 id="iii-epic-does-not-belong-to-the-hero-alone" tabindex="-1">III. Epic Does Not Belong to the Hero Alone <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-epic-does-not-belong-to-the-hero-alone" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Epic Does Not Belong to the Hero Alone&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory-faction civilizations&#39; epics are often &quot;hero epics&quot; — the protagonist&#39;s lone legend. Heng Yuan Zhou deliberately opposes this:</p><ul><li>The Quest Domain records epics whose protagonist is <strong>the Myriad-Race collective</strong>, not some individual.</li><li>Lin Hao, Anchor Council members&#39; contributions will be recorded, but the focus is &quot;how Myriad Ranks walked through together,&quot; not &quot;some king&#39;s martial prowess.&quot;</li><li>This is precisely anti-predation axiom&#39;s extension in civilizational memory: <strong>even epics do not allow individual monopolization</strong>.</li></ul><h2 id="iv-epic-prevents-civilization-from-repeating-tragedy" tabindex="-1">IV. Epic Prevents Civilization from Repeating Tragedy <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-epic-prevents-civilization-from-repeating-tragedy" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Epic Prevents Civilization from Repeating Tragedy&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Epic transmission&#39;s most practical function is <strong>preventing historical reversal</strong> (the predatory faction&#39;s common disease repeatedly argued in Module Two):</p><ul><li>The Quest Domain makes Tang-Luo-style monopoly, Shrouding-style solitary Dao, Perfect-World-style decisively monopolizing eternity etc. old systems&#39; failures into &quot;reverse-side epics.&quot;</li><li>Later generations in instances personally experience the cost of these failures, emotionally understand &quot;why cannot go back.&quot;</li><li>This emotional-level warning more than any legal provision prevents civilization from repeating old mistakes.</li></ul><p>The Quest Domain is therefore civilization&#39;s &quot;immune memory&quot; — turning past illness into future antibodies.</p><h2 id="supplementary-argument-epic-is-civilization-s-immune-gene" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Argument: Epic Is Civilization&#39;s &quot;Immune Gene&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-argument-epic-is-civilization-s-immune-gene" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Argument: Epic Is Civilization&#39;s &quot;Immune Gene&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilization, like people, forgets; because it forgets old wounds, it repeats them. The Quest Sediment Domain records and transmits epics, essentially writing an &quot;immune gene&quot; into civilization — making Tang-Luo-style monopoly, Shrouding-style solitary Dao, decisively-monopolizing-eternity&#39;s cost into scars later generations have emotionally experienced. Emotional memory is more stubborn than legal provisions: a young person who wept for Tang-Luo-style victims in an instance, as an adult, will never easily endorse new monopoly. This alert born from emotional depths cannot be exchanged by any external coercion. Epic transmission is therefore not nostalgia, but civilization&#39;s gentlest yet strongest vaccine against historical reversal.</p><h2 id="brief-transition" tabindex="-1">Brief Transition <a class="header-anchor" href="#brief-transition" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Brief Transition&quot;">​</a></h2><p>These epics are not only stored in the Quest Sediment Domain; their abstracted values and lessons, through the Alaya Network, continuously flow to the Origin Acceleration Domain&#39;s R&amp;D personnel, reminding them whom technology explosion should serve. The slow track&#39;s memory is the fast track&#39;s compass that never goes off course.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: sediment predecessors&#39; sacrifices and lessons into epics; do not burn history for nothing</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: epics record Myriad-Race collective; do not sing individual predatory heroes</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s epic is the protagonist&#39;s personal legend; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s epic is Myriad Ranks&#39; shared memory</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: five lineages&#39; experiences all recorded in epics; no one&#39;s付出 forgotten</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: epic instances, value textbooks network-wide open; newly merged planes may learn Myriad Ranks&#39; historical wisdom</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="addendum" tabindex="-1">Addendum <a class="header-anchor" href="#addendum" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Addendum&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilizational epics are therefore completely different from personal biographies: it records how Myriad Ranks walked through together, not how some king was martial. Every technical leap of the Origin Acceleration Domain, every emotional resonance of the Quest Sediment Domain, ultimately converges into the long river of epic, becoming the land under later generations&#39; feet.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Technology explosion lets civilization run fast; epic transmission lets civilization run far. A civilization without epics, no matter how fast, only circles in place — it does not know why it set out, so it does not know where to go. The Quest Sediment Domain, with slowness, installs &quot;memory and direction&quot; on the wild-running technology explosion. Fast civilizations run faster in speed; slow epics outlast time — dual-track unified, civilization can be both fast and far.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/05-万族共进基本纲领.html">Entry 05 · Myriad-Race Joint Progress Basic Program</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/87-仅回传知识原则.html">Entry 87 · Only-Knowledge-Returned Principle</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/70-纪元划分总表.html">Entry 70 · Era Division Master Table</a> · <a href="./628_模块3-时间域文明升维-加速域技术爆炸.html">Entry 628 · Acceleration-Domain Technology Explosion</a></li></ul>',32)])])}const p=i(a,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
